@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.795 = private unnamed_addr constant [599 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `debug=True` in Flask.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AEnabling debug mode shows an interactive debugger in the browser if an\0Aerror occurs, and allows running arbitrary Python code from the browser.\0AThis could leak sensitive information, or allow an attacker to run\0Aarbitrary code.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport flask\0A\0Aapp = Flask()\0A\0Aapp.run(debug=True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport flask\0A\0Aapp = Flask()\0A\0Aapp.run(debug=os.environ[\22ENV\22] == \22dev\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Flask documentation: Debug Mode](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/latest/quickstart/#debug-mode)\0A", align 1
