@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.800 = private unnamed_addr constant [652 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstrings that are written via f-strings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython will interpret the f-string as a joined string, rather than as a\0Adocstring. As such, the \22docstring\22 will not be accessible via the\0A`__doc__` attribute, nor will it be picked up by any automated\0Adocumentation tooling.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    f\22\22\22Not a docstring.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    \22\22\22A docstring.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [Python documentation: Formatted string literals](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-strings)\0A", align 1
